# AI visual geolocation — estimate a photo's location from pixel content when it
# has no GPS/place metadata. Provider-agnostic: any OpenAI-compatible vision API.
#
# Default = Groq (FREE). Just set the key (GROQ_API_KEY also accepted):
VISION_API_KEY=
# Optional overrides (defaults shown) to switch provider/model:
# VISION_BASE_URL=https://api.groq.com/openai/v1
# VISION_MODEL=meta-llama/llama-4-scout-17b-16e-instruct
#
# Example — Google Gemini free tier (stronger vision):
# VISION_API_KEY=<aistudio key>
# VISION_BASE_URL=https://generativelanguage.googleapis.com/v1beta/openai
# VISION_MODEL=gemini-2.0-flash

# Metadata geolocation (EXIF GPS, IPTC/XMP place tags) + OpenStreetMap geocoding
# + reverse image search + Instagram geo-pivot links remain fully free and need
# no keys. Without VISION_API_KEY the app still works from EXIF GPS + place tags
# alone (no AI pixel-content estimate).

# Reverse image search hosts the uploaded image on a public host (catbox.moe) so
# Yandex/Lens can match it to its original (often geotagged) post. Set to 0 to
# disable if the subject image must not leave your control.
# REVERSE_IMAGE_UPLOAD=1

# The map (incl. Satellite 3D buildings + terrain) is 100% free and needs NO key:
# Esri World Imagery, OpenFreeMap vectors, and AWS terrarium elevation tiles.
